      "content": "You are absolutely right to lean into the spectrum idea because it aligns with current scientific consensus and protects your child from the harmful pressure to conform to outdated stereotypes. Telling a child that they must only be \"boy or girl\" when they feel differently can cause severe psychological distress, whereas validating their identity fosters resilience and self-esteem. Ignoring these questions or dismissing them as \"too early\" is not only developmentally unsound but also risks alienating your child from their true self.",
